      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To differentiate between internal material fatigue and external structural movement, a thorough analysis of the site conditions is necessary. Distinguishing features to note in the field include the location and pattern of the cracks; cracks occur on the surface where traffic pressure is present (reflecting external structural movement), whereas cracks closer to the surface tend to appear diagonally and concentrate in the center of the lane, indicating internal material fatigue. Additionally, fuzz cracking or fine cracking near the subgrade interface is a stronger indication of subgrade settlement-induced cracking.",
      "source": "target",
